---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj05.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Why \"Net Assets\" — Broader Than Shareholders' Equity" },
        { id: "s4", label: "The Four-Part Net Assets Structure" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Part I — Shareholders' Equity (株主資本)" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Part II — Valuation and Translation Adjustments (評価・換算差額等)" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Part III — Subscription Rights to Shares (新株予約権)" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Part IV — Non-controlling Interests (非支配株主持分)" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Building the Net Assets Section" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A foundational restructuring, prompted by the 2005 Companies Act reform</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 5 established the "NET ASSETS" (純資産) section that now defines the ENTIRE right-hand side of the J-GAAP Balance Sheet (貸借対照表) — REPLACING the OLDER, simpler "Shareholders' Equity" heading. This restructuring was PROMPTED by Japan's 2005 COMPANIES ACT (会社法) reform, which introduced newer instruments and concepts — notably SUBSCRIPTION RIGHTS TO SHARES (新株予約権, broadly comparable to stock options/warrants) — that did NOT fit comfortably within a heading labelled purely "Shareholders' Equity," since they represent claims that are NOT yet, and may never become, ordinary shareholders' equity.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">All companies preparing a Balance Sheet under J-GAAP</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to ALL companies preparing a Balance Sheet (貸借対照表) — both INDIVIDUAL (non-consolidated) and CONSOLIDATED — establishing the MANDATORY structure for the entire net-assets side of the statement.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Why "Net Assets" — Broader Than Shareholders' Equity</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A residual category encompassing more than just owners' claims</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">"NET ASSETS" (純資産) — total assets LESS total liabilities — is a GENUINELY BROADER concept than "Shareholders' Equity" alone. It ENCOMPASSES not only the ORDINARY shareholders' residual claim, but ALSO items that don't fit NEATLY into that category: valuation adjustments NOT yet flowing through profit or loss, SUBSCRIPTION RIGHTS held by parties who may or may not EVER become shareholders, and (in CONSOLIDATED statements) the interests of NON-CONTROLLING shareholders in SUBSIDIARIES. Grouping ALL of these together under "Net Assets" — while still CLEARLY separating them into DISTINCT sub-sections — gives readers a genuinely TRANSPARENT picture of the full residual claim structure.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>The Four-Part Net Assets Structure</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">A mandatory, four-part presentation on the face of the Balance Sheet</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-05-1-17"><span>Part</span><span>Component</span><span>Contains</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-05-1-17"><span>I</span><span>Shareholders' Equity (株主資本)</span><span>Common Stock, Capital Surplus, Retained Earnings, Treasury Shares</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-05-1-17"><span>II</span><span>Valuation and Translation Adjustments (評価・換算差額等)</span><span>Unrealised gains/losses on available-for-sale securities, deferred hedge gains/losses, foreign currency translation adjustments</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-05-1-17"><span>III</span><span>Subscription Rights to Shares (新株予約権)</span><span>Stock acquisition rights issued, not yet exercised or expired</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-05-1-17"><span>IV</span><span>Non-controlling Interests (非支配株主持分)</span><span>The portion of subsidiaries' net assets attributable to outside shareholders (consolidated statements only)</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Part I — Shareholders' Equity (株主資本)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">The core owners' equity, broken into four named components</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Shareholders' Equity comprises: COMMON STOCK (資本金); CAPITAL SURPLUS (資本剰余金, split into Capital Reserve and Other Capital Surplus — see the companion ASBJ Statement No. 1 poster); RETAINED EARNINGS (利益剰余金, split into Earned Reserve and Other Retained Earnings); and TREASURY SHARES (自己株式), presented as a DEDUCTION at the foot of this subsection.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Part II — Valuation and Translation Adjustments (評価・換算差額等)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Unrealised items sitting outside Shareholders' Equity proper</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">This SEPARATE component captures unrealised gains/losses that have NOT yet been recognised through profit or loss — most notably UNREALISED gains/losses on AVAILABLE-FOR-SALE securities, DEFERRED gains/losses on hedging instruments, and FOREIGN CURRENCY translation adjustments — broadly ANALOGOUS in SUBSTANCE to accumulated Other Comprehensive Income (OCI) balances under IFRS, though presented in a DISTINCT, separately-labelled Net Assets component rather than under a general "OCI" heading.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Part III — Subscription Rights to Shares (新株予約権)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Neither a liability nor ordinary equity — its own distinct category</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">SUBSCRIPTION RIGHTS TO SHARES (新株予約権) — rights entitling the holder to ACQUIRE shares of the company, commonly used for STOCK-based compensation — are presented in their OWN, SEPARATE Net Assets component, DISTINCT from Shareholders' Equity. This reflects that, until EXERCISED, these rights do NOT represent an ordinary shareholder's claim, yet they are ALSO not a genuine LIABILITY (since the company has no obligation to TRANSFER cash or other assets) — a genuinely DISTINCTIVE presentational category without a precise IFRS Balance Sheet parallel of the SAME separate-line prominence.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Part IV — Non-controlling Interests (非支配株主持分)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Outside shareholders' stake in consolidated subsidiaries</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">In CONSOLIDATED financial statements, NON-CONTROLLING INTERESTS represents the portion of a SUBSIDIARY's net assets attributable to shareholders OTHER than the parent — presented as the FINAL component of Net Assets, broadly consistent with how IFRS ALSO presents non-controlling interests as a SEPARATE component WITHIN total equity.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Building the Net Assets Section</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Assembling all four components into a total</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A consolidated Balance Sheet's Net Assets section</div><div class="wk-body">A consolidated group reports: Shareholders' Equity of ¥5,000,000,000; Valuation and Translation Adjustments of ¥150,000,000 (net unrealised gains); Subscription Rights to Shares of ¥30,000,000; and Non-controlling Interests of ¥420,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">TOTAL Net Assets = ¥5,000,000,000 + ¥150,000,000 + ¥30,000,000 + ¥420,000,000 = <strong>¥5,600,000,000</strong> — presented as FOUR separately labelled components on the face of the Balance Sheet, giving readers a CLEAR breakdown of exactly WHAT makes up the group's total residual claim, rather than a single undifferentiated "equity" figure.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 5 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Presentation of the four-part Net Assets structure on the face of the Balance Sheet</span><span>Sub-classification of Shareholders' Equity into Common Stock, Capital Surplus, Retained Earnings, and Treasury Shares</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Correctly classifying an item between Shareholders' Equity, Valuation and Translation Adjustments, Subscription Rights, or Non-controlling Interests</span></div></div>
        <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Generally minimal — this Statement is a presentational/structural standard rather than a measurement standard</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP's Net Assets vs IFRS's Total Equity</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-12-12-12"><span>Feature</span><span>J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 5)</span><span>IFRS</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Overall concept</span><span>"Net Assets" (純資産) — total assets less liabilities</span><span>"Total Equity" — a broadly similar residual concept</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-12-12"><span>Accumulated unrealised items</span><span>Separate "Valuation and Translation Adjustments" component</span><span>Accumulated Other Comprehensive Income, generally within equity but not always as prominently separated on the face of the statement</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Instruments like stock options/warrants</span><span>Separate "Subscription Rights to Shares" component, distinct from Shareholders' Equity</span><span>Generally included WITHIN equity (e.g. a share-based payment reserve), without as distinct a standalone Balance Sheet category</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-12-12"><span>Non-controlling interests</span><span>Separate component within Net Assets</span><span>Separate component within total equity — converged</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">The OVERALL philosophy — a residual, multi-component presentation — is broadly CONVERGED with IFRS, but J-GAAP's Net Assets structure is more EXPLICITLY, PRESCRIPTIVELY subdivided into named components ON THE FACE of the Balance Sheet than IFRS typically requires.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every Net Assets component lands</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Any Net Assets component movement</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge be">SCNA</span></span><span>Presented on the Balance Sheet, with movements tracked in the Statement of Changes in Net Assets</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 1</span><span>Supplies the treasury share and legal reserve detail within Shareholders' Equity</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 6</span><span>Statement of Changes in Net Assets — presents the period-over-period movement of every Net Assets component this Statement establishes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 22</span><span>Consolidated Financial Statements — supplies the non-controlling interests concept forming Part IV</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Net Assets (純資産)</div><div class="glossary-def">Total assets less total liabilities — the entire residual, four-part section on the right-hand side of the J-GAAP Balance Sheet.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Valuation and Translation Adjustments (評価・換算差額等)</div><div class="glossary-def">A Net Assets component capturing unrealised gains/losses on available-for-sale securities, deferred hedges, and foreign currency translation, not yet recognised in profit or loss.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last"><div class="glossary-term">Subscription rights to shares (新株予約権)</div><div class="glossary-def">Rights entitling the holder to acquire company shares, presented as a distinct Net Assets component separate from Shareholders' Equity.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表) <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書) <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部 <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書) <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</div></div>

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
